+# Daily Grind
+
+Run `npm start` with Node.js 20 or newer to serve the homepage and signup API.
+`PORT` defaults to `11222`; `HOST` defaults to `0.0.0.0`.
+
+The homepage posts JSON `{ "email": "you@example.com" }` to
+`POST /api/newsletter`. Valid signups are appended to `data/newsletter.jsonl`.
+Set `NEWSLETTER_DATA_FILE` to a persistent, writable path when deploying.
+The data directory is excluded from Git and is never served by the server.
+This collects newsletter subscriptions; it does not send campaign emails.
+
+Every response includes an enforced Content Security Policy. Scripts and styles
+must come from this server; fetch requests and form submissions are same-origin.
+Images may come from this server or `https://images.unsplash.com`. Other resource
+sources, inline scripts, inline event handlers, frames, plugins, and base URL
+overrides are blocked. There are no external runtime dependencies or build step.
+
+The signup displays pending, success, validation, server, network, and timeout
+feedback in a live region. Blocked connection, form, and image requests also
+produce a security message. A successful response is sent only after storage
+completes.
